# The coefficients of the product of two polynomials of coefficients of one limb that the program
# supplies (milestone2.md, "sum, dot, axpy, convolution": conv_k): conv_1 with the coefficients by
# dot_1_entry, whose step guards both factors (rule R3, the factors of a fused operation:
# architecture.md). conv_1's step only multiplies the coefficients; but a compiler that sees one
# polynomial to hold ones fuses a product the program stored into the other into it (Apple clang 21
# under -ffp-contract=fast at -O2 with NDEBUG, measured: every round). Two additions more per term,
# and the statement of conv_1 holds of the values in the arrays whatever the compiler does. Its
# claims are those of conv_1.
fold:          conv_1_entry
arrays:        supplied x, supplied y
coefficients:  dot_1_entry
state:         mask finite
combine:       finite = and(finite, finite)
orders:        sequential
writes:        z
check:         fold_finish_1
finish:        none
value:         x*y
ensures:       coefficients z
ensures:       finite_or_nan z flag=finite
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/FoldConv.v
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeFoldConv.v
terms_theorem: proofs/theories/FoldConv.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        dot_1_entry on the terms of each coefficient
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
